{
 "slug": "relative-image-width",
 "module": "relative-image-width/src/size",
 "function": "parseSize",
 "note": "Each case names its function in fn. parseSize(token) gives the CSS width and height of a size token W or WxH, or null when it is not a size or has no relative unit (core sizes pixels). A percent height maps to vh. splitAlt(alt) splits caption|size. parsePandocAttrs(text) reads {#id .class width= height=}. findPandocAttrs(line) gives the offsets of a block directly after a link to an image file. isImageLink(link) tells if the link target has an image file extension. defaultSize(setting, property) is the Pro default size. Names that start with a number are acceptance groups 1 to 7 of SPEC.md. Reviewed by hand against each input.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "1 percent width",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "50%"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "50%",
    "height": null
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "2 percent width and percent height maps height to vh",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "50%x30%"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "50%",
    "height": "30vh"
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "2 post 1 form 50%x50%",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "50%x50%"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "50%",
    "height": "50vh"
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "3 em width",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "70em"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "70em",
    "height": null
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "3 rem width",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "20rem"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "20rem",
    "height": null
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "3 vw width",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "40vw"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "40vw",
    "height": null
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "3 vh width",
   "fn": "parseSize",
   "args": [
    "30vh"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "width": "30vh",
    "height": null
   }
  },
  {
